<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108172" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπογάστρ-ιον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the lower belly from the
				navel downwards, the paunch,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				4.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				503a17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.48
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the belly of a sea-fish,</i> esp. of the tunny, a favourite
			dish at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Stratt.
				4
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				31
			</span></i> (hex.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				364
			</span></i>, etc.; whence the joke in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>V.</u>
				195
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
